"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[88418],{88418:function(r){r.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n## Linux DRM - Core Initialization and Driver Registration\\n```require\\n- Kernel: Based on Linux v6.19 source\\n- Prerequisite: Linux DRM Part 1: Architecture and Overview\\n```\\n### Introduction\\n| Part | Topic |\\n|---|---|\\n| Part 1 | <a href=\\"/posts/content/2026-10-26-post-linux-drm-01-architecture\\">Architecture and Overview</a> |\\n\\nIn Part 1, we examined the structure of DRM (`drm_driver` → `drm_device` → `drm_minor` → `drm_file`) and device nodes. In this post, we will trace <b>how this structure is created in code</b> across two stages: the DRM core reserving major number 226 at boot time, and a driver (here, the virtual driver <b>vkms</b>) creating the device and registering `/dev/dri/card0` and `renderD128`.  \\n\\n\\n```adcard\\n```\\n\\n### Code Flow 1: DRM Core Initialization\\nDRM is initialized once when the kernel boots. This is where major number 226, which we saw earlier, gets registered.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c - drm_core_init() (L1236-1272)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nstatic int __init drm_core_init(void)\\n{\\n\\tint ret;\\n\\n\\tdrm_connector_ida_init();\\n\\tdrm_memcpy_init_early();\\n\\n\\tret = drm_sysfs_init();  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret < 0) {\\n\\t\\tDRM_ERROR(\\"Cannot create DRM class: %d\\\\n\\", ret);\\n\\t\\tgoto error;\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tdrm_debugfs_init_root();\\n\\tdrm_debugfs_bridge_params();\\n\\n\\tret = register_chrdev(DRM_MAJOR, \\"drm\\", &drm_stub_fops);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret < 0)\\n\\t\\tgoto error;\\n\\n\\tret = accel_core_init();\\n\\tif (ret < 0)\\n\\t\\tgoto error;\\n\\n\\tdrm_panic_init();\\n\\n\\tdrm_privacy_screen_lookup_init();\\n\\n\\tdrm_core_init_complete = true;\\n\\n\\tDRM_DEBUG(\\"Initialized\\\\n\\");\\n\\treturn 0;\\n\\nerror:\\n\\tdrm_core_exit();\\n\\treturn ret;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L1236-L1272\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c L1236-L1272</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\n`drm_sysfs_init()` creates the `/sys/class/drm` class, and <mark>register_chrdev(DRM_MAJOR, \\"drm\\", &drm_stub_fops)</mark> creates the `226 drm` line in `/proc/devices`. At this point, no device exists yet. DRM has merely reserved the entire major number 226 and registered a <b>single \\"stub\\" file operations structure that intercepts every open()</b>.  \\n\\n### Code Flow 2: The Driver Registers the Device\\nNow it is time for the driver to step in. Let\'s look at vkms. First, here is the `drm_driver` defined by the driver.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.c - vkms_driver (L92-102)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nstatic const struct drm_driver vkms_driver = {\\n\\t.driver_features\\t= DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_ATOMIC | DRIVER_GEM,  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t.fops\\t\\t\\t= &vkms_driver_fops,  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tDRM_GEM_SHMEM_DRIVER_OPS,\\n\\tDRM_FBDEV_SHMEM_DRIVER_OPS,\\n\\t.name\\t\\t\\t= DRIVER_NAME,\\n\\t.desc\\t\\t\\t= DRIVER_DESC,\\n\\t.major\\t\\t\\t= DRIVER_MAJOR,\\n\\t.minor\\t\\t\\t= DRIVER_MINOR,\\n};\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.c#L92-L102\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.c L92-L102</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\n`DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_ATOMIC | DRIVER_GEM` and `fops` created via `DEFINE_DRM_GEM_FOPS` are all it takes. The function that registers this driver is `vkms_create()`.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.c - vkms_create() (L159-220)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nint vkms_create(struct vkms_config *config)\\n{\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tdev_name = vkms_config_get_device_name(config);\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tvkms_device = devm_drm_dev_alloc(&fdev->dev, &vkms_driver,  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t struct vkms_device, drm);\\n\\tif (IS_ERR(vkms_device)) {\\n\\t\\tret = PTR_ERR(vkms_device);\\n\\t\\tgoto out_devres;\\n\\t}\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tret = drm_vblank_init(&vkms_device->drm,  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\t\\t      vkms_config_get_num_crtcs(config));\\n\\tif (ret) {\\n\\t\\tDRM_ERROR(\\"Failed to vblank\\\\n\\");\\n\\t\\tgoto out_devres;\\n\\t}\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tret = vkms_modeset_init(vkms_device);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto out_devres;\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tret = drm_dev_register(&vkms_device->drm, 0);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto out_devres;\\n\\n\\tdrm_client_setup(&vkms_device->drm, NULL);\\n\\t/* ... */\\n}\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.c#L159-L220\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.c L159-L220</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\n\\n```adcard\\n```\\n\\n```mermaid\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Driver Registration Flow (Based on vkms)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nsequenceDiagram\\n    participant D as Driver (vkms_create)\\n    participant C as DRM core\\n    participant S as sysfs \xb7 devtmpfs \xb7 udev\\n    D->>C: devm_drm_dev_alloc(&vkms_driver)\\n    C->>C: drm_dev_init()<br/>drm_minor_alloc(RENDER, PRIMARY)<br/>drm_gem_init()\\n    D->>C: drm_vblank_init()\\n    D->>C: vkms_modeset_init()<br/>(Register planes \xb7 CRTCs \xb7 connectors)\\n    D->>C: drm_dev_register()\\n    C->>C: drm_minor_register(RENDER)<br/>drm_minor_register(PRIMARY)\\n    C->>S: device_add(minor->kdev)\\n    S-->>S: /dev/dri/card0 (226:0)<br/>/dev/dri/renderD128 (226:128)\\n```\\n#### Step 1: Allocation and Initialization (drm_dev_init)\\n`devm_drm_dev_alloc()` invokes `drm_dev_init()` via internal `devm_drm_dev_init()`. Here, it <mark>creates minors based on driver_features</mark> and initializes GEM.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c - drm_dev_init() (L701-796)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nstatic int drm_dev_init(struct drm_device *dev,\\n\\t\\t\\tconst struct drm_driver *driver,\\n\\t\\t\\tstruct device *parent)\\n{\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tkref_init(&dev->ref);\\n\\tdev->dev = get_device(parent);\\n\\tdev->driver = driver;\\n\\n\\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->managed.resources);\\n\\tspin_lock_init(&dev->managed.lock);\\n\\n\\tdev->driver_features = ~0u;  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->filelist);\\n\\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->filelist_internal);\\n\\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->clientlist);\\n\\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->client_sysrq_list);\\n\\tINIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->vblank_event_list);\\n\\n\\tspin_lock_init(&dev->event_lock);\\n\\tmutex_init(&dev->filelist_mutex);\\n\\tmutex_init(&dev->clientlist_mutex);\\n\\tmutex_init(&dev->master_mutex);\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tif (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_COMPUTE_ACCEL)) {\\n\\t\\tret = drm_minor_alloc(dev, DRM_MINOR_ACCEL);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\t\\tgoto err;\\n\\t} else {\\n\\t\\tif (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_RENDER)) {\\n\\t\\t\\tret = drm_minor_alloc(dev, DRM_MINOR_RENDER);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\t\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tgoto err;\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tret = drm_minor_alloc(dev, DRM_MINOR_PRIMARY);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\t\\tgoto err;\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_GEM)) {\\n\\t\\tret = drm_gem_init(dev);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tif (ret) {\\n\\t\\t\\tDRM_ERROR(\\"Cannot initialize graphics execution manager (GEM)\\\\n\\");\\n\\t\\t\\tgoto err;\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tdev->unique = drmm_kstrdup(dev, dev_name(parent), GFP_KERNEL);\\n\\tif (!dev->unique) {\\n\\t\\tret = -ENOMEM;\\n\\t\\tgoto err;\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tdrm_debugfs_dev_init(dev);\\n\\t/* ... */\\n}\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L701-L796\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c L701-L796</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\nIf `DRIVER_RENDER` is set, it allocates a render minor, and it always allocates a primary minor. `drm_minor_alloc()`, which allocates a minor, picks a minor number (`xa_alloc`) and prepares the `struct device` (`kdev`) for sysfs.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c - drm_minor_alloc() (L142-172)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nstatic int drm_minor_alloc(struct drm_device *dev, enum drm_minor_type type)\\n{\\n\\tstruct drm_minor *minor;\\n\\tint r;\\n\\n\\tminor = drmm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*minor), GFP_KERNEL);\\n\\tif (!minor)\\n\\t\\treturn -ENOMEM;\\n\\n\\tminor->type = type;\\n\\tminor->dev = dev;\\n\\n\\tr = xa_alloc(drm_minor_get_xa(type), &minor->index,  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\t     NULL, DRM_MINOR_LIMIT(type), GFP_KERNEL);\\n\\tif (r == -EBUSY && (type == DRM_MINOR_PRIMARY || type == DRM_MINOR_RENDER))\\n\\t\\tr = xa_alloc(&drm_minors_xa, &minor->index,  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\t\\t     NULL, DRM_EXTENDED_MINOR_LIMIT, GFP_KERNEL);\\n\\tif (r < 0)\\n\\t\\treturn r;\\n\\n\\tr = drmm_add_action_or_reset(dev, drm_minor_alloc_release, minor);\\n\\tif (r)\\n\\t\\treturn r;\\n\\n\\tminor->kdev = drm_sysfs_minor_alloc(minor);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (IS_ERR(minor->kdev))\\n\\t\\treturn PTR_ERR(minor->kdev);\\n\\n\\t*drm_minor_get_slot(dev, type) = minor;\\n\\treturn 0;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L142-L172\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c L142-L172</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\n\\n```adcard\\n```\\n\\n#### Step 2: Registration (drm_dev_register)\\nOnce the driver has prepared all KMS objects, it calls <mark>drm_dev_register()</mark>. From this point onward, userspace can open the device.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c - drm_dev_register() (L1056-1126)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nint drm_dev_register(struct drm_device *dev, unsigned long flags)\\n{\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tif (!driver->load)  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tdrm_mode_config_validate(dev);\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tret = drm_minor_register(dev, DRM_MINOR_RENDER);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto err_minors;\\n\\n\\tret = drm_minor_register(dev, DRM_MINOR_PRIMARY);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto err_minors;\\n\\n\\tret = drm_minor_register(dev, DRM_MINOR_ACCEL);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto err_minors;\\n\\n\\tret = create_compat_control_link(dev);\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto err_minors;\\n\\n\\tdev->registered = true;\\n\\t/* ... */\\n\\tif (driver->load) {  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tret = driver->load(dev, flags);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\t\\tgoto err_minors;\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tif (drm_core_check_feature(dev, DRIVER_MODESET)) {\\n\\t\\tret = drm_modeset_register_all(dev);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\t\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\t\\tgoto err_unload;\\n\\t}\\n\\tdrm_panic_register(dev);\\n\\tdrm_client_sysrq_register(dev);\\n\\t/* ... */\\n}\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L1056-L1126\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c L1056-L1126</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\n`drm_minor_register()` registers the device with sysfs via `device_add()` and populates the minor number table (`xa_store`). Later, `open()` uses this table to look up the minor.  \\n\\n```c\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c - drm_minor_register() (L174-212)\\"\\n}\\n---\\nstatic int drm_minor_register(struct drm_device *dev, enum drm_minor_type type)\\n{\\n\\tstruct drm_minor *minor;\\n\\tvoid *entry;\\n\\tint ret;\\n\\n\\tDRM_DEBUG(\\"\\\\n\\");\\n\\n\\tminor = *drm_minor_get_slot(dev, type);\\n\\tif (!minor)\\n\\t\\treturn 0;\\n\\n\\tif (minor->type != DRM_MINOR_ACCEL) {\\n\\t\\tret = drm_debugfs_register(minor, minor->index);\\n\\t\\tif (ret) {\\n\\t\\t\\tDRM_ERROR(\\"DRM: Failed to initialize /sys/kernel/debug/dri.\\\\n\\");\\n\\t\\t\\tgoto err_debugfs;\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tret = device_add(minor->kdev);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (ret)\\n\\t\\tgoto err_debugfs;\\n\\n\\tentry = xa_store(drm_minor_get_xa(type), minor->index, minor, GFP_KERNEL);  // [!code highlight]\\n\\tif (xa_is_err(entry)) {\\n\\t\\tret = xa_err(entry);\\n\\t\\tgoto err_debugfs;\\n\\t}\\n\\tWARN_ON(entry);\\n\\n\\tDRM_DEBUG(\\"new minor registered %d\\\\n\\", minor->index);\\n\\treturn 0;\\n\\nerr_debugfs:\\n\\tdrm_debugfs_unregister(minor);\\n\\treturn ret;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n> **Source** <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L174-L212\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c L174-L212</a> (Linux v6.19)\\n\\n### Code Locations\\n| Step | Function | Location (Linux v6.19) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Boot: DRM core initialization (Register major number 226) | `drm_core_init()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L1236-L1272\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c:1236</a> |\\n| Boot: Stub open (Swap fops) | `drm_stub_open()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L1188-L1216\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c:1188</a> |\\n| Driver: Device allocation and minor creation | `drm_dev_init()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L701-L796\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c:701</a> |\\n| Driver: Minor number and sysfs device | `drm_minor_alloc()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L142-L172\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c:142</a> |\\n| Driver: card%d / renderD%d naming | `drm_sysfs_minor_alloc()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_sysfs.c#L551-L591\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_sysfs.c:551</a> |\\n| Driver: Registration (Create /dev/dri nodes) | `drm_dev_register()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L1056-L1126\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c:1056</a> |\\n| Driver: Register minor with sysfs | `drm_minor_register()` | <a href=\\"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.19/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c#L174-L212\\" target=\\"_blank\\">drivers/gpu/drm/drm_drv.c:174</a> |\\n\\n\\n```adcard\\n```\\n\\n### Summary\\nHere is what we covered in this post:  \\n\\n- <b>Core initialization</b>: `drm_core_init()` registers major number 226 and sets up stub fops to intercept all `open()` calls.\\n- <b>Driver registration</b>: Through `devm_drm_dev_alloc()` → `drm_dev_init()` (minor number allocation) → `drm_dev_register()` → `drm_minor_register()` → `device_add()`, `/dev/dri/card0` and `renderD128` are created.\\n\\nNow that the nodes are available, it\'s time for userspace to make use of them. Next, we will explore how <b>`open()` and `ioctl()`</b> are handled inside the kernel."}')}}]);